              "ev-d714a1b62f8b-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Kenneth N. Flaxman, the case presents the Court with a question similar to that addressed in Heck v. Humphrey, but in a slightly different context."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d714a1b62f8b16071d355dabd116723dfb542eb6b21236b2b2225b86a0666e5b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d714a1b62f8b-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice GINSBURG, justice Ginsburg stated that the Seventh Circuit said damages would run only from the time of the allegedly unlawful arrest until the time of arraignment, and that without an arraignment no damages would be attributed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d714a1b62f8b16071d355dabd116723dfb542eb6b21236b2b2225b86a0666e5b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d714a1b62f8b-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked Mr. Flaxman whether this case should be treated like Heck, focusing on the line between \u00a71983 and habeas corpus."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d714a1b62f8b16071d355dabd116723dfb542eb6b21236b2b2225b86a0666e5b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d714a1b62f8b-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens, justice Stevens questioned whether the rule would create an incentive for defendants to file \u00a71983 actions in every criminal case."
      }
    ],
