  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Kenneth N. Flaxman",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d714a1b62f8b16071d355dabd116723dfb542eb6b21236b2b2225b86a0666e5b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d714a1b62f8b-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Kenneth N. Flaxman, the case concerns the timing of accrual for \u00a71983 claims arising from unlawful arrests, referencing the question addressed in Heck v. Humphrey in a slightly different context."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. FLAXMAN",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d714a1b62f8b16071d355dabd116723dfb542eb6b21236b2b2225b86a0666e5b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d714a1b62f8b-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. FLAXMAN, petitioner argues that under Seventh Circuit precedent the cause of action for a \u00a71983 claim starts at the time of arrest or, alternatively, at arraignment (or a Gerstein probable\u2011cause hearing)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. SOLOMON",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d714a1b62f8b16071d355dabd116723dfb542eb6b21236b2b2225b86a0666e5b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d714a1b62f8b-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. SOLOMON, respondent officers contend that a rule of delayed accrual would undermine the purposes of the statute of limitations and that every victim of a Fourth Amendment violation should be entitled to damages."
      }
    ],
